## Evidence

<!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line MD044 -->
<!-- jig-ignore-next-line: Markdown link target is indivisible -->
The accepted [faithful-base governance ADR](../../../adr/governance/faithful-base-and-optional-mod-boundary.md)
defines the complete admission set for canonical base changes: deterministic
conversion of validated source, a required Unreal/target representation change,
import/runtime correctness required to reproduce source behavior, or correction
of a defect introduced by SHAR itself. Every admitted change must keep source
fact, conversion rule, and result distinguishable.

The policy fails closed on missing or contradictory evidence and explicitly
states that an editor session, AI suggestion, screenshot, aesthetic preference,
convenience heuristic, or third-party mod is not source authority. Existing P1
conversion audits remain responsible for proving any disputed transform or asset
correction before it can enter base output.
